<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="defs_P_14_3" targetNamespace="http://tim-method.example/utility-wam/1.0" exporter="Utility WAM Industry Process Reference" exporterVersion="2026-08-28">
  <process id="P_14_3" name="14.3 Capture and approve time" isExecutable="false">
    <documentation>All four processes are drawn, and the group is one path because time only moves one way: captured at the work, cascaded to the people who did it, corrected by them, approved by a supervisor, and released.

TIME IS RECORDED AGAINST THE WORK, NOT AGAINST THE DAY, and that single choice is what makes 5.2.1 possible. A daily total cannot be settled to a work order, and 5.2.1 is where the cost of the work actually lands. The flow therefore starts from the assignment rather than from the shift.

OFFLINE IS THE NORMAL CASE, NOT AN EXCEPTION, and it is drawn as a hold rather than as an error path. Field work happens where there is no connectivity. What the device does while disconnected, and how it resolves a sync conflict, are entirely vendor-defined - the reference specifies WHAT is captured and is silent on how the device behaves, because no standard reaches it.

THE CASCADE RUNS AGAINST THE CREW AS CONSTITUTED, not as planned. A planned crew that differs from the actual one produces time for people who were not there, and that only surfaces at 14.4.4 if it surfaces at all.

A CORRECTION RETAINS THE ORIGINAL. Overwriting time already settled to a work order breaks the cost record with nothing left to reconcile against, and 5.2.5 then has an exception with no history. The reopen path is drawn, and the path for a period already sent to payroll deliberately is not - that is 14.4.4's, because 14.3.3 must never look as though it can undo a payment.</documentation>
    <laneSet id="P_14_3_lanes">
      <lane id="l_143_field" name="Field capture">
        <flowNodeRef>n_143_start</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_143_cap</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_143_conn</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_143_hold</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_143_crew</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_143_casc</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_143_pres</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_143_edit</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_143_reason</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_143_sub</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
      <lane id="l_143_appr" name="Approval">
        <flowNodeRef>n_143_test</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_143_dec</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_143_back</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_143_rel</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_143_end</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
    </laneSet>
    <startEvent id="n_143_start" name="A worker records time against work"><messageEventDefinition id="n_143_start_md"/></startEvent>
    <userTask id="n_143_cap" name="Record time against the work order and task"><documentation>14.3.1. Against the WORK, not the day. Capturing the type and premium triggers here is what lets 14.4.1 value it later.</documentation></userTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_143_conn" name="Device connected"/>
    <receiveTask id="n_143_hold" name="Hold locally until connectivity returns"><documentation>14.3.1. The normal case. Offline behaviour and sync conflict resolution are vendor-defined; the reference does not specify them.</documentation></receiveTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_143_crew" name="Entered for a crew"/>
    <serviceTask id="n_143_casc" name="Cascade to the crew as constituted"><documentation>14.3.2. As CONSTITUTED, not as planned. Each member's entry must stand alone afterwards, with its own type and exceptions.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <userTask id="n_143_pres" name="Present the period back to the worker"><documentation>14.3.3. Before anyone approves it.</documentation></userTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_143_edit" name="Edits made"/>
    <serviceTask id="n_143_reason" name="Record the edit with its reason"><documentation>14.3.3. An unexplained edit is indistinguishable from an error and from a manipulation, and the difference matters where hours drive a premium.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <sendTask id="n_143_sub" name="Submit the timesheet"><documentation>14.3.3.</documentation></sendTask>
    <businessRuleTask id="n_143_test" name="Test against the operator's exception rules"><documentation>14.3.4. The rules are the operator's - no standard defines what an anomalous timesheet looks like.</documentation></businessRuleTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_143_dec" name="Approve, query or reject"/>
    <sendTask id="n_143_back" name="Return for correction with the reason"><documentation>14.3.4. Back to 14.3.3, which retains the original entry.</documentation></sendTask>
    <sendTask id="n_143_rel" name="Release approved time to costing and to pay"><documentation>14.3.4. The same hours go to 5.2.1 as work cost and to 14.4.3 as pay. Approving them separately is how the two stop reconciling.</documentation></sendTask>
    <endEvent id="n_143_end" name="Time approved and released"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_143_start_n_143_cap" sourceRef="n_143_start" targetRef="n_143_cap" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_143_cap_n_143_conn" sourceRef="n_143_cap" targetRef="n_143_conn" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_143_conn_n_143_hold" sourceRef="n_143_conn" targetRef="n_143_hold" name="offline"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[connected = false]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_143_hold_n_143_crew" sourceRef="n_143_hold" targetRef="n_143_crew" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_143_conn_n_143_crew" sourceRef="n_143_conn" targetRef="n_143_crew" name="connected"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_143_crew_n_143_casc" sourceRef="n_143_crew" targetRef="n_143_casc" name="crew entry"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[crewEntry = true]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_143_casc_n_143_pres" sourceRef="n_143_casc" targetRef="n_143_pres" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_143_crew_n_143_pres" sourceRef="n_143_crew" targetRef="n_143_pres" name="individual entry"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_143_pres_n_143_edit" sourceRef="n_143_pres" targetRef="n_143_edit" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_143_edit_n_143_reason" sourceRef="n_143_edit" targetRef="n_143_reason" name="edited"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[edited = true]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_143_reason_n_143_sub" sourceRef="n_143_reason" targetRef="n_143_sub" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_143_edit_n_143_sub" sourceRef="n_143_edit" targetRef="n_143_sub" name="unchanged"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_143_sub_n_143_test" sourceRef="n_143_sub" targetRef="n_143_test" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_143_test_n_143_dec" sourceRef="n_143_test" targetRef="n_143_dec" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_143_dec_n_143_back" sourceRef="n_143_dec" targetRef="n_143_back" name="queried or rejected"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_143_back_n_143_pres" sourceRef="n_143_back" targetRef="n_143_pres" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_143_dec_n_143_rel" sourceRef="n_143_dec" targetRef="n_143_rel" name="approved"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_143_rel_n_143_end" sourceRef="n_143_rel" targetRef="n_143_end" name=""/>
  </process>
